# PT-82 (architect's ruling, process/cairn/issues/PT-82.md @ 6316a9b,
# item (a)3): gitignored files a fresh worktree needs for the dashboard
# to build, copied in on EnterWorktree. Only files that are BOTH gitignored
# AND matched by a pattern here are copied — and for a wholly-ignored
# directory (node_modules/ is ignored wholesale, .gitignore:28), a `**/`
# pattern does NOT reach inside it; the directory must be named explicitly.
# Measured, not guessed — do not "simplify" this back to `**/node_modules/**`.
scripts/cairn/dashboard/node_modules/**
# Spike delta 1, then delta 3 (process/reviews/PT-82/spike.md @ 1d25274,
# 643dd89): `node_modules/.bin/` is a dot-directory of SYMLINKS -- naming
# it explicitly here (as this comment used to) still did not deliver it
# on a repeat, measured twice. The worktree-copy mechanism does not
# preserve this dot-directory of symlinks, so this is NOT a pattern
# problem to keep chasing. Fix moved to the build itself instead:
# package.json's `build` script invokes vite directly
# (`node ./node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build`), which needs only the
# `vite` package directory (delivered by the pattern above), never the
# `.bin/` symlink.
